# System color scheme

Theme follows `prefers-color-scheme`. No in-app light/dark toggle unless the user asks for one.

- Put new colors in `src/canvas/styles.css` as CSS variables. Add both the light `:root` value and the `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` value in the same change.
- Paint with tokens (`var(--bg)`, `var(--ink)`, `var(--panel)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--accent)`, shadows, `--iframe-bg`). Do not hardcode light-only hex in canvas CSS or renderer-created elements.
- Keep `color-scheme: light dark` on `:root` and `<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">` on canvas HTML shells.
- Preview iframes use the mock app’s own system theme. Do not force the iframe to light.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.node { background: #fffdf8; border-color: #d6d3d1; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.node { background: var(--panel); border-color: var(--border); }
```
